<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to September 4 as released by the Bank of Japan on Wednesday:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.35 (0.35)	 one year     0.46 (0.51)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.35 (0.35)	 two years    0.75 (0.86)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.40 (0.43)	 three years  1.30 (1.40)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.31)	 one year     0.42 (0.46)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.31 (0.31)	 two years    0.70 (0.81)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.35 (0.39)	 three years  1.25 (1.36)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million</p>
<p>yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.26 (0.26)	 one year     0.38 (0.42)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.26 (0.27)	 two years    0.65 (0.76)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.31 (0.34)	 three years  1.20 (1.31)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Sept 2 - Sept 6:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.49 (0.50)   120-150 days  UNQ  (0.60)</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.54 (0.54)   150-180 days  UNQ  (UNQ )</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.54 (0.57)   180-360 days  0.60 (0.62)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.54 (0.58)   over 360 days 0.70 (0.80)</p>
</text>
